Carbine! We're attacking the power-deficit device!

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:41.140
Start acceleration!

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.370
Start the engine right now!

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.020
I'll be right back!

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:07.190
All of the Euronelph facilities have been restarted!

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:07.730
We're going back!

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:39.500
Maen, thank you for your hard work.

00:13:41.890 --> 00:13:46.400
Winning is complete. Misato, come and pick up the luggage.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.660
Roger that. We will descend to the recovery point from now on.

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:54.190
We prioritize the recovery preparation of the crew.

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:55.850
Put down all the recovery-involved ships.

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:59.180
We need to go to the front of the ship.

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:04.020
Saikuwa Ryuryu

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:09.370
With this, you can modify the heart of the Nikoichi type 2 and the overlapping sun type 8.

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:18.380
I'll be sure to pick you up wherever you are, so wait for me, Wanko-kun.

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:02.870
Tch, I'm not brave enough.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:15.370
Sorry, I'm late.

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:17.830
Are you okay, Ikari?

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:23.760
If you go from there, I'll find out.

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:29.090
Oh, you're awake.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:35.490
You don't know me? I'm Toji, Suzuhara Toji.

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:38.050
It's been a long time, Shinji.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:40.370
I was surprised when you were brought in.

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:44.670
I've heard a little about you, but I don't know much about you.

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:46.820
Anyway, I'm glad you're doing well.

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:49.740
So, can you move now?

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:56.500
That's right.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:58.040
Then let's go home.

00:16:58.220 --> 00:16:59.280
You must be hungry.

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:03.300
It's a little cold outside.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:06.310
She doesn't want to change.

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.030
Well, it's okay as it is.

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:11.260
And the camiflora is about to die.

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:13.230
Okay, I'll talk to the branch manager.

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:16.360
I'm sorry, but I'm going to go up with this today.

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:18.240
Let's go.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:41.440
There are a lot of strange people.

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:42.890
What? Is this the first time there's been a crowd?

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:46.030
This is one of the villages where the survivors gathered.

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:48.170
It's the third village.

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:50.090
About a thousand people live here.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.130
That's the food distribution center.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.750
Three times a week, they decide the date and distribute it.

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:56.520
Teacher, hello.

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:58.480
Oh, Matsukata-san.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:17:59.350
You're almost there.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:00.640
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:03.940
Teacher, those two are the ones who took care of the credit.

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.540
Well, that's fine.

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:08.160
I'm counting on you.

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:08.740
Yeah.

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.210
Well then, excuse me.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:11.090
Oh!

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:14.470
What's a credit?

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:19.270
A credit is a support organization created by Vire.

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:20.130
It's not just for the supply.

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:22.340
It also helps with the trade between this village and other villages.

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:26.550
Our village alone can't live very well.

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:29.000
What's that?

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:31.160
The shape of the dog is different.

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.290
Huh? That's a cat.

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:34.500
Cat?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.430
Is it your first time seeing a cat?

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:39.350
There are about 20 cats living under the car.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.360
I'm happy that there are only dogs and cats here.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:47.200
This is my old but fun house.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.140
I'll make it a luxury house.

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:52.950
I'll prepare dinner soon.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:02.650
Thanks for waiting. Let's eat while it's still hot.

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:06.180
Shinji, you must be hungry. You should eat something.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:11.400
Well, if you want to eat, come here anytime.

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:12.420
Here you go.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:14.370
Thank you for the food.

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:18.000
It's good, isn't it?

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:20.880
The inside of the blood is strange. It's warm.

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.230
That's right. That's what's good.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.000
My daughter has a good tongue.

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:29.150
Really. She's the best wife in the world.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.180
I'll be surprised if you do.

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:34.130
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:36.750
Oh, welcome back. I've been waiting for you.

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:38.580
Shinji, do you know?

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.190
She's my wife.

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:41.620
She's the chairman.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:44.380
I couldn't believe it when I got the call.

00:19:44.900 --> 00:19:46.880
Even if I'm in front of you like this, it's still like a dream.

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:48.880
It's been a long time, Ikari-kun.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.180
Ayanami-san, too.

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:52.330
No, I'm not Ayanami.

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:53.380
What?

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:54.370
Is that wrong?

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.050
Then...

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:56.930
You look just like her.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:02.140
What's this?

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:05.260
It's our daughter, Tsubame.

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:05.980
Isn't she cute?

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:07.500
She's small even though she's human.

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:09.200
Why did you make her so small?

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:10.360
What's this?

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:11.080
Is this the first time you've seen a baby?

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:14.150
She's even smaller when she's born.

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.400
Babies grow bigger and bigger.

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:28.170
Isn't she cute?

00:20:28.190 --> 00:20:29.120
Isn't she cute?

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.930
She's our daughter after all!

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:36.800
I was so surprised.

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:39.550
Manzuba...

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.190
Did I make her cry?

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:45.160
That's my job!

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.860
Sorry, I'm late.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:48.910
Oh!

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:56.510
Are you crying?

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:59.160
The baby is growing up after drinking his father's water.

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:12.630
I don't know what to do if it's Ayanami Rei.

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:17.020
You're different from Ayanami-san, aren't you?

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:19.270
Then you can do what you think.

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:25.070
It's okay to be different.

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:29.880
It's been a long time since I've seen it.

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:29.960
Thank you for watching until the end.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.130
That's right, Ikari. It's Aida. Aida Kensuke.

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:34.350
Yes.

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:38.280
That's right, Kensuke.

00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:40.330
I'm going to help you.

00:21:40.710 --> 00:21:43.500
We've been helped a lot by this survival otaku.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:48.320
If it wasn't for him, we would have been lost a long time ago.

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:55.890
Shinji, don't say anything.

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.700
But eat the food you were given.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:58.810
That's polite.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.130
Dad, I shouldn't have invited you to dinner.

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:06.190
I was just being nice to you today.

00:22:06.370 --> 00:22:07.690
But, Toji-kun.

00:22:07.850 --> 00:22:09.420
You don't even have to eat a bite of this precious meal.

00:22:11.460 --> 00:22:14.080
Right, Shinji-kun?

00:22:14.380 --> 00:22:20.580
Let's go to the party.

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:23.520
You and Ikari-kun too.

00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:26.120
No, I'll take care of Ikari.

00:22:26.180 --> 00:22:27.620
That would be better.

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:36.250
It was unexpected, wasn't it?

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:41.020
The reason I married the chairman at that time was because we were always fighting in junior high school.

00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:45.050
Well, the trigger was the Nia Third Impact.

00:22:45.980 --> 00:22:47.640
After that, we had a long relationship.

00:22:47.960 --> 00:22:53.160
Ikari, Nia is not just a bad thing.

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:12.840
If you climb up this hill, you'll be there soon.

00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:20.450
Ikari, we're here.

00:23:22.340 --> 00:23:24.480
It's a self-built house using the ruins of Mujin Station.

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:25.610
Use it as you like.

00:23:25.890 --> 00:23:27.370
The toilet is in the back of the vehicle.

00:23:27.830 --> 00:23:29.870
I'll get the fuel, so go ahead.

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:30.740
Please come in.

00:23:30.740 --> 00:23:39.780
I'm naked.

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:42.400
Why don't you explain it to me and make me happy?

00:23:42.920 --> 00:23:47.590
Ken-Ken also picked up such a troublesome guy.

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:48.690
He likes things.

00:23:49.130 --> 00:23:50.120
I'm home.

00:23:50.260 --> 00:23:52.700
Oh, it's a guest.

00:23:52.960 --> 00:23:54.740
I think he'll be at home for a while.

00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:58.120
There is a situation, and Shikinami can't show his face to the village.

00:23:58.400 --> 00:23:59.180
Not really.

00:23:59.180 --> 00:23:59.720
Thank you for watching.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.480
It's just annoying because there are so many Kirin.

00:24:01.480 --> 00:24:11.940
Only the PSS Joker has a reaction.

00:24:12.400 --> 00:24:17.950
Ken-Ken, you're too kind to him.

00:24:18.250 --> 00:24:19.820
Let him blow it himself.

00:24:20.260 --> 00:24:22.210
Ikari doesn't eat now.

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:23.910
I can't do anything by myself.

00:24:23.970 --> 00:24:24.970
It must have been so hard.

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:27.380
That's not always the case.

00:24:27.720 --> 00:24:29.290
Close your heart like that.

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:31.840
It's his way to survive, isn't it?

00:24:31.860 --> 00:24:33.660
Just leave him alone.

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:36.820
He doesn't want to live anyway, but he doesn't want to die anyway.

00:24:37.460 --> 00:24:41.040
Ikari, that's enough for now.

00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:43.100
It's a good thing to reunite like this.

00:24:43.800 --> 00:24:45.500
You can rely on me as much as you want.

00:24:45.580 --> 00:24:47.320
We're friends, aren't we?

00:24:47.340 --> 00:24:49.520
I'm happy that Ikari is alive.

00:24:50.680 --> 00:24:51.080
President!

00:24:56.720 --> 00:24:58.900
I don't like you.

00:25:01.660 --> 00:25:02.820
Thank you for your hard work every day.

00:25:02.920 --> 00:25:04.730
Good night, Hanate.

00:25:04.750 --> 00:25:06.840
What's a good night?

00:25:07.970 --> 00:25:09.410
That's right.

00:25:09.610 --> 00:25:11.960
It's a magic spell for everyone to sleep in peace.

00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:15.200
Good night, Sokkuri-san.

00:25:41.360 --> 00:25:42.620
I'm tired of pretending to sleep.

00:25:42.940 --> 00:25:45.450
When will I be able to sleep?

00:26:19.840 --> 00:26:21.960
It's a magic to live together with everyone.

00:26:21.960 --> 00:26:23.860
Good morning, Sokkuri-san.

00:26:30.480 --> 00:26:31.660
KenKen gets up at 6 no matter what day it is.

00:26:32.380 --> 00:26:33.670
He's already going to work.

00:26:33.870 --> 00:26:35.270
You can have breakfast there.

00:26:35.530 --> 00:26:36.830
Hurry up and eat!

00:26:40.150 --> 00:26:43.330
You're a great, neat-looking girl, aren't you?

00:26:43.510 --> 00:26:44.270
I'm Sokkuri-san, who was asked by my teacher's wife.

00:26:45.710 --> 00:26:46.870
Nice to meet you from today.

00:26:47.030 --> 00:26:48.010
Sokkuri-san?

00:26:48.430 --> 00:26:50.190
It's a name that seems to have something to do with it.

00:26:50.470 --> 00:26:51.310
Is it okay to put honey in it?

00:26:52.090 --> 00:26:52.980
It doesn't matter if you put it on your skin.

00:26:54.180 --> 00:26:57.820
If it's an order, I'll do it.

00:26:57.940 --> 00:26:59.880
It's not an order, it's a job.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:01.410
What is work?

00:27:02.450 --> 00:27:03.390
What do you mean what?

00:27:03.570 --> 00:27:05.300
I've never thought about it.

00:27:06.060 --> 00:27:07.870
Well, it means that everyone will shed sweat.

00:27:09.110 --> 00:27:10.670
Sweat.

00:27:11.350 --> 00:27:13.180
Lightly with the index finger.

00:27:13.940 --> 00:27:14.320
Yes.

00:27:14.680 --> 00:27:16.770
I don't think I'll put it deep from the top.

00:27:21.870 --> 00:27:22.330
Just add the fingers.

00:27:23.350 --> 00:27:24.970
I have no choice but to get used to it.

00:27:33.480 --> 00:27:33.740
See?

00:27:35.230 --> 00:27:44.240
This is Asemizu.

00:27:44.630 --> 00:27:45.110
Huh?

00:27:51.010 --> 00:27:54.090
It's a job.

00:27:55.810 --> 00:27:57.730
Ahaha, it's a mess.

00:27:58.050 --> 00:27:59.210
It can't be helped.

00:28:00.320 --> 00:28:01.420
I'll lend you my hand.

00:28:02.040 --> 00:28:08.300
Thank you for your hard work.

00:28:08.540 --> 00:28:10.180
You've been working hard again today.

00:28:11.020 --> 00:28:14.240
This is special because I worked hard on the first day.

00:28:15.140 --> 00:28:19.170
Doki, what should I say?

00:28:20.260 --> 00:28:20.900
Thank you.

00:28:22.560 --> 00:28:25.900
Everyone, let's go to the bath.

00:28:26.300 --> 00:28:27.310
What is a bath?

00:28:32.750 --> 00:28:33.510
This is a bath.

00:28:37.660 --> 00:28:38.920
You'll be in trouble if you keep wearing it.

00:28:39.820 --> 00:28:47.810
It's strange.

00:28:48.090 --> 00:28:50.710
It's not like LCL, it's warm.

00:28:51.390 --> 00:28:56.840
I'm alive even though I don't have an order.

00:29:00.190 --> 00:29:04.500
Shut up and lie down on the corner.

00:29:05.440 --> 00:29:07.860
You just want to appeal that you're in pain, don't you?

00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:09.660
You're in the way of cleaning.

00:29:09.700 --> 00:29:11.000
You're really annoying.

00:29:11.590 --> 00:29:27.390
You were a good boy.

00:29:31.440 --> 00:29:32.740
Thank you for everything, Hikari!

00:29:32.880 --> 00:29:35.200
It's okay. We're both happy to do this.

00:29:35.240 --> 00:29:36.980
Let's go home.

00:29:37.560 --> 00:29:37.900
Yeah.

00:29:44.560 --> 00:29:46.740
A magic trick to meet again?

00:29:46.760 --> 00:29:56.260
A magic trick to get better?

00:30:13.850 --> 00:30:19.730
It's hard for us too, but...

00:30:31.180 --> 00:30:33.690
I'm so grateful that you let me eat like this!

00:30:36.310 --> 00:30:37.530
You're still like a lily!

00:30:37.830 --> 00:30:39.270
You can't live without eating!

00:30:39.470 --> 00:30:40.310
So eat!

00:30:40.630 --> 00:30:41.990
This is just water!

00:30:42.350 --> 00:30:44.030
Before you become a body that doesn't change anything,

00:30:44.110 --> 00:30:45.250
taste the badness of food!

00:30:45.930 --> 00:30:46.470
You idiot!

00:30:47.440 --> 00:30:49.740
Just because you don't do anything like that

00:30:49.740 --> 00:30:52.280
doesn't mean you don't want to get hurt again, right?

00:30:52.600 --> 00:30:53.740
If you have time,

00:30:53.860 --> 00:30:55.040
at least at that time,

00:30:55.100 --> 00:30:56.820
I'll beat you up!

00:31:00.190 --> 00:31:05.650
You two are too weak!

00:31:05.950 --> 00:31:08.660
You guys have been jealous of each other,

00:31:08.920 --> 00:31:10.220
and now you can't get back at each other.

00:31:10.680 --> 00:31:12.030
It's all your fault,

00:31:12.130 --> 00:31:13.650
so you don't want to do anything anymore, right?

00:31:14.110 --> 00:31:15.900
Even if it's what your parents say,

00:31:16.520 --> 00:31:18.230
if you have such mental strength,

00:31:18.470 --> 00:31:21.080
I don't want you to ride the Eva in the first place!

00:31:45.160 --> 00:31:46.040
You're all alone, aren't you, Teruki?

00:33:00.860 --> 00:33:02.720
I'm home. Oh, where's Ikari?

00:33:02.940 --> 00:33:04.500
She went home.

00:33:04.760 --> 00:33:08.910
I see. I guess it's best to leave her alone for now.

00:33:09.890 --> 00:33:10.900
Where's she going?

00:33:11.220 --> 00:33:12.770
To the ruins of Hida Lake.

00:33:14.190 --> 00:33:14.930
That's not a good place for a Nerf facility.

00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:18.330
Where's Leishon?

00:33:18.550 --> 00:33:21.040
I forced her to eat. She'll be here for a while.

00:33:21.600 --> 00:33:23.340
Thank you, Shikinami.

00:33:23.960 --> 00:33:25.740
Not really. It's not her fault.

00:33:26.140 --> 00:33:27.840
I won't forgive myself for dying on my own.

00:33:30.090 --> 00:33:44.850
My name?

00:33:45.530 --> 00:33:47.380
Yeah, you can't always be the same.

00:33:49.040 --> 00:33:51.820
You seem to have forgotten your own name.

00:33:52.900 --> 00:33:55.220
Why don't you make a new one yourself?

00:33:56.790 --> 00:33:59.260
Can I make a new name?

00:34:32.590 --> 00:34:33.690
I picked it up, so I'll give it back to you.

00:34:33.750 --> 00:34:36.070
Thank you.

00:34:36.190 --> 00:34:38.170
Want me to read it?

00:34:38.390 --> 00:34:41.580
Thank you.

00:34:41.740 --> 00:34:53.480
I'm alone.

00:34:53.740 --> 00:34:57.900
Until now, and from now on, I'll always be alone.

00:34:59.480 --> 00:34:59.820
That's it.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:00.820
Of course, it's a bus.

00:35:01.400 --> 00:35:01.760
Who?

00:35:07.940 --> 00:35:10.320
It's me.

00:35:10.400 --> 00:35:12.110
It's a first-class pilot.

00:35:12.330 --> 00:35:15.070
I'm going to open the door now.

00:35:15.190 --> 00:35:19.180
I heard Hikari-kun was here.

00:35:19.980 --> 00:35:21.090
He's not here.

00:35:21.130 --> 00:35:22.190
He's at home.

00:35:22.570 --> 00:35:24.970
Then I'll look for him.

00:35:25.370 --> 00:35:26.640
I'll tell you.

00:35:27.740 --> 00:35:29.540
We Eva pilots are the same as Eva.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:31.500
In order not to exceed the human frame, it is restricted during design.

00:35:32.560 --> 00:35:34.520
It also has inefficient emotions.

00:35:35.320 --> 00:35:36.910
It's just designed to match people's cognitive behavior.

00:35:38.350 --> 00:35:42.400
The Ayanami series is adjusted so that the third boy has a good intention.

00:35:43.480 --> 00:35:47.180
My current feelings have been instilled in NERV from the beginning.

00:35:47.560 --> 00:35:51.580
Yes, but it's okay. I feel good.

00:35:52.460 --> 00:35:59.740
If so, if you do it yourself, your target is NERV's second division, N109.

00:35:59.740 --> 00:35:59.980
Thank you for watching.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.800
Thank you.

00:36:01.800 --> 00:36:05.000
If you're going to go to him, take the ration there.

00:36:05.460 --> 00:36:06.580
It's almost the limit.

00:36:07.040 --> 00:36:09.960
Do you stay in this village and don't work?

00:36:10.620 --> 00:36:11.800
Are you stupid?

00:36:12.100 --> 00:36:13.620
This is not where I am.

00:36:14.300 --> 00:36:15.520
It's a place to protect.

00:36:34.160 --> 00:36:34.900
I'll return what I've picked up.

00:36:35.320 --> 00:36:36.390
I was taught.

00:37:06.780 --> 00:37:07.260
I'll be back.

00:38:12.440 --> 00:38:13.440
and conviction

00:38:13.440 --> 00:38:14.960
of my thought

00:38:14.960 --> 00:38:17.020
I will

00:38:17.490 --> 00:38:18.130
oversee

00:38:18.130 --> 00:38:18.790
the

00:38:21.950 --> 00:38:26.090
I've been

00:38:26.090 --> 00:38:26.430
here

00:38:29.460 --> 00:38:29.760
I've been

00:38:37.770 --> 00:38:38.910
Trust in my death.

00:39:08.280 --> 00:39:10.540
That I'll never see the day

00:39:33.450 --> 00:39:50.320
Shinji, are you sure you'll be fine by yourself?

00:39:50.580 --> 00:39:52.090
If you keep it up, you'll be in trouble.

00:39:53.110 --> 00:39:54.410
Let's leave it at that for now.

00:39:54.470 --> 00:39:56.410
Ikari needs that kind of time.

00:39:57.190 --> 00:39:58.910
But, Kensuke...

00:40:00.280 --> 00:40:01.400
Is Shinji too cold?

00:40:02.510 --> 00:40:04.730
It's not good to worry too much about each other.

00:40:04.830 --> 00:40:06.130
I'll be back.

00:40:06.510 --> 00:40:07.480
I'll wait for Shinji.

00:40:08.710 --> 00:40:09.530
That's right.

00:40:09.730 --> 00:40:13.450
I hope Shinji gets used to this village as soon as possible.

00:40:14.450 --> 00:40:23.780
Why don't you go back to the village?

00:40:24.040 --> 00:40:29.340
Kari, do you have anything to say here?

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:32.950
I don't care. Are you also someone who protects this village?

00:40:33.390 --> 00:40:40.130
I'm not protecting it. I'm the one who destroyed everything.

00:40:40.560 --> 00:40:43.640
I don't want to do anything anymore. I don't want to talk to anyone.

00:40:43.940 --> 00:40:45.180
Don't come to me anymore!

00:40:45.380 --> 00:40:48.420
I want you to leave me alone!

00:40:48.700 --> 00:40:54.990
I'm kind to everyone!

00:41:01.980 --> 00:41:09.150
Thank you for talking to me. This is a magic trick to get along with you.

00:41:09.650 --> 00:41:28.680
It's over at home.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:35.130
Thanks to you, I cried as much as I could.

00:41:35.170 --> 00:41:36.260
Did you feel refreshed?

00:41:36.840 --> 00:41:42.680
If you can move now,

00:41:43.160 --> 00:41:44.500
you can help Ken-Ken.

00:41:45.260 --> 00:41:56.330
Sometimes driving is good, right?

00:41:56.450 --> 00:41:57.500
It's a change of mood.

00:42:00.030 --> 00:42:02.510
I have been allowed to do agricultural work as a machine industry.

00:42:02.910 --> 00:42:03.990
I don't care about anything.

00:42:04.290 --> 00:42:06.950
Today, the main job is to check the external infrastructure and the environment.

00:42:08.190 --> 00:42:09.200
I'm busy.

00:42:09.600 --> 00:42:14.460
However, the existing infrastructure has almost stopped due to life.

00:42:14.460 --> 00:42:16.930
It's hard to repair, so I'm leaving it.

00:42:17.390 --> 00:42:28.940
Are the branches falling?

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:31.100
I only use the ones with branches.

00:42:31.560 --> 00:42:33.020
I want to take care of the remaining forest.

00:42:35.060 --> 00:42:42.360
The living base of the third village depends on the water here.

00:42:43.180 --> 00:42:44.860
The water supply here is important.

00:42:45.610 --> 00:42:49.450
It is the water of life that is directly related to the survival problem of the village.

00:42:49.830 --> 00:42:53.340
I will look at the water source ahead.

00:42:53.760 --> 00:42:56.980
The road to Ikari is tight, so please work here.

00:42:57.260 --> 00:42:59.270
I ask you to procure food with this.

00:43:00.890 --> 00:43:03.900
I can't do it. I've never done it, and I can't do it.

00:43:04.180 --> 00:43:06.350
It's okay. Say it after you've done it.

00:43:06.850 --> 00:43:11.840
Well, don't worry about it.

00:43:11.980 --> 00:43:13.610
We have one per week.

00:43:14.190 --> 00:43:14.900
There's another one.

00:43:15.300 --> 00:43:20.720
That's a souvenir from Ville.

00:43:20.820 --> 00:43:22.560
It's a white device that corrects the L barrier.

00:43:24.900 --> 00:43:28.050
Thanks to that, the third village doesn't live in fear.

00:43:28.050 --> 00:43:28.910
I'm living without being scared.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:30.940
It's all thanks to you, Mr. Kusato.

00:43:31.360 --> 00:43:37.420
I've been seeing it lately.

00:43:37.600 --> 00:43:38.570
It's broken with the disassembly.

00:43:40.020 --> 00:43:41.800
The long-hidden Eva

00:43:41.800 --> 00:43:43.540
It started to move all of a sudden.

00:43:44.720 --> 00:43:45.880
That's how it is today.

00:43:45.980 --> 00:43:49.740
After all, it won't come in through the seal.

00:43:49.820 --> 00:43:51.800
It also works against disassembly.

00:43:53.490 --> 00:43:54.750
There's something I can't do.

00:43:55.250 --> 00:43:57.050
If that stops, it's a deal.

00:44:01.690 --> 00:44:04.020
As you can see, I don't know how long I'm going to stay here.

00:44:05.140 --> 00:44:09.940
But until then, I'm going to live my life to the fullest.

00:44:09.980 --> 00:44:12.180
That's a plum.

00:44:12.600 --> 00:44:15.190
My husband is looking forward to eating it every year.

00:44:15.990 --> 00:44:19.730
Living is a repetition of hard and fun things.

00:44:20.610 --> 00:44:22.650
It's okay if every day is the same as today.

00:44:22.990 --> 00:44:24.190
That's how it is.

00:44:25.370 --> 00:44:29.170
Now is the youngest time in my life, and I want to live now.

00:44:30.410 --> 00:44:31.310
There's a swallow, too.

00:44:31.570 --> 00:44:36.590
She's more affectionate than I am.

00:44:36.910 --> 00:44:39.660
I wish Sokkuri-san would stay here forever.

00:44:40.140 --> 00:44:43.650
My name?

00:44:43.990 --> 00:44:44.230
Yeah.

00:44:44.640 --> 00:44:45.810
Have you decided yet?

00:44:46.050 --> 00:44:48.150
No, I haven't decided yet.

